title: 'FRAME: preserve constants from multiple extra_constants blocks'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Pallets can define multiple `#[pallet::extra_constants]` blocks. All blocks now contribute
    constants to metadata in declaration order, after the constants defined in `Config`, instead
    of silently keeping only the last block. Bounds and instance usage are checked across all
    blocks. Rebuild the runtime and regenerate metadata bindings to expose previously omitted
    constants. Pallets using a single block retain their existing metadata.
crates:
- name: frame-support-procedural
  bump: patch
- name: frame-support
  bump: patch
